RESPOND inside TRANSACTION commits the transaction and sends the response;
THROW HTTPERROR inside TRANSACTION rolls back the transaction (Requirements 6.7, 9.5).

### empty at start
GET /notes
=> 200

[]

### RESPOND inside TRANSACTION commits
POST /notes

{"text": "first", "amount": "12.50"}
=> 201

{"id": 1, "text": "first", "amount": "12.50"}

### THROW HTTPERROR inside TRANSACTION rolls back
POST /notes/fail

{"text": "rolled back", "amount": "99.00"}
=> 422

{"error": "NOTE REJECTED"}

### only the committed row is present
GET /notes
=> 200

[{"id": 1, "text": "first", "amount": "12.50"}]
